# IndiaLens — Engineering Rules

Quantitative education and career intelligence platform. Two deployables:

- `indialens/` — Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind
- `backend/` — FastAPI, SQLAlchemy (async), ML stack

---

## Non-negotiable: data honesty

This platform tells students how much a degree costs and what it earns. A
fabricated number here is worse than a missing one — it is advice someone
makes a ₹40L decision on.

- **Never substitute a constant for a missing measurement.** No
  `medianSalary ?? 1_200_000`, no `placementRate ?? 88`, no `networkScore ?? 88`.
  Pass `null` through and render an explicit "no data" state.
- The same applies to scoring. If a score has no backing column, it is `null`,
  not a plausible default. When aggregating, average only over measured inputs
  and reweight — never treat a missing input as a zero or a midpoint.
- `backend/db/schema.sql` is the record of what is actually known. When the DB
  has no value, say so in the UI rather than inventing one.
- `backend/tests/test_security_config.py::TestNoFabricatedData` enforces this.
  Do not weaken those assertions to make a change pass.

## Security

- **RLS is the boundary.** `anon` is unauthenticated and the anon key ships in
  the client bundle. Any policy on a table holding student PII must be scoped
  by token or session — `USING (true)` grants the whole table. CI blocks it.
- `student_reports`, `personal_intelligence`, `portfolio_profiles` are
  student-owned. Writes go through the backend with the service-role key.
- Student data is read with `fetchSupabaseRest(..., { reportToken })`, which
  sets the `x-report-token` header the RLS policies match on. Omitting it on a
  read of those tables silently returns zero rows.
- **Never commit credentials.** Env files are gitignored. `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` is
  client-visible by design; everything else is server-only. CI runs a secret
  scan.
- `backend/api/config.py` refuses to boot in production with a placeholder or
  under-length secret. Do not weaken that validator to make a deploy work.
- `SECURITY DEFINER` views bypass RLS. Use `security_invoker`.

## Auth

- Google ID tokens must validate `aud` against the configured client id and
  require `email_verified`. A verification failure returns 401 — never fall
  through to an unauthenticated path.
- Compare secrets with `secrets.compare_digest`, not `==`.
- **Payments are out of scope.** `upgrade_to_premium` trusts the request body
  and is not a working billing system. Do not build on it or treat it as one.

## Data access architecture

Two paths exist and are being consolidated **backend-first**:

- `indialens/src/lib/supabase.ts` → PostgREST, anon key (client)
- `indialens/src/lib/backend.ts` → FastAPI (server)

Prefer the FastAPI path for anything student-owned or privileged. Direct
PostgREST reads are acceptable for the public catalogue
(`colleges`, `degrees`, `programs`, `roi_scores`, `global_programs`) and must
stay read-only.

## Testing

- Backend: `cd backend && python -m pytest` (66 tests). `pytest.ini` sets
  `pythonpath`, so it works from `backend/` or the repo root.
- Frontend typecheck: `cd indialens && npx tsc --noEmit`
- Every behaviour change ships with a test that fails without the fix.
  Security fixes in particular — that is how the last round shipped undetected.
- `next.config.mjs` sets `ignoreBuildErrors` and `ignoreDuringBuilds` to true,
  so a broken build will not fail locally. Typecheck explicitly; do not trust
  `npm run build` alone.

## Conventions

- Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `security:`, `test:`, `docs:`).
  No `[AI-CoLab: ...]` tags — they make `git blame` useless.
- Optional chaining on API-derived arrays (`rec.reasons?.map(...)`) — the
  Gemini and analytics responses are not schema-validated at runtime.
- `ruff check` for Python; the CI `python-check` job runs it.
- Never push to `main`. Branch, open a PR, let the required checks
  (`type-check`, `python-check`, `Vercel – vivdhedu-1`) gate the merge.

## Deployment

- Frontend deploys from the repo root with Vercel `rootDirectory = indialens`.
  Locally, run `vercel` commands from the repo root, not from `indialens/`,
  or the root directory is applied twice.
- Required Vercel env vars: `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`,
  `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`. They are not
  optional — the build fails at prerender without them.
- `vivdhedu-1` is the live project. `vivdhedu-1-47pi` is a duplicate of the
  same repo on the same production branch and should be deleted.
